-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX B.
--
-- A nearer inner-section binding must shadow a farther same-named ancestor even
-- when the inner binding is a FORWARD reference to a not-yet-inferred
-- un-annotated DECIDE (its type is still an unresolved inference variable).
--
-- Previously, because candidates were grouped by type BEFORE proximity was
-- considered, the inner `bonus` (unknown type) and the outer `bonus` (NUMBER)
-- fell into different type groups and were never compared by proximity,
-- producing a spurious, order-dependent AmbiguousTermError. Proximity must win:
-- `usage` sees the inner `bonus` (5), so `usage` is 6.

§ a
bonus MEANS 20

§§ inner
usage MEANS bonus PLUS 1    -- forward reference to the inner `bonus` below
bonus MEANS 5

#EVAL usage    -- 6
